{
  "area": "indirect",
  "about": "INDIRECT (docs/specs/exsheet-functions ticket 18; ADR-0124's note of 2026-10-10): A1-style text naming a cell or a range of the same Sheet, with or without its own qualifier, read as it stands after the recalculation (volatile). Its text is not rewritten by an insertion or a deletion. The forms the seventeenth Windows run observed are read as Excel reads them: R1C1 text (a1 FALSE, 0, a blank or left empty) naming an absolute cell or a range of two, a structured reference's text as the typed Table[Column] is read, and A1# as the typed A1# is. R1C1 text in a relative form or naming whole rows or columns is #VALUE! until a run observes it; text that names no place, another Sheet's name and a table or column that does not exist included, is #REF!.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "INDIRECT-001",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "Microsoft's example: the Value of the cell A2's text names (B2)",
      "cells": {"A2": "B2", "A3": "B3", "A4": "George", "A5": "5", "B2": "1.333", "B3": "45", "B4": "10", "B5": "62", "ZZ1000": "=INDIRECT(A2)"},
      "check": "ZZ1000",
      "expect": {"value2": 1.333}
    },
    {
